WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.480
Question sixteen.

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:08.529
Step one: macro scan. It asks what most likely happens when a bitmap is enlarged.

00:00:08.529 --> 00:00:11.923
One mark. Command words: “most likely”.

00:00:11.923 --> 00:00:13.490
Step two: denoise.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:17.842
Useful, in yellow: bitmap, enlarged several times.

00:00:17.842 --> 00:00:19.843
In cyan: “most likely”.

00:00:19.843 --> 00:00:25.065
Useless red herring: art class, outdoor print — kick it out.

00:00:25.065 --> 00:00:26.632
Step three: draft.

00:00:26.632 --> 00:00:28.808
A bitmap is a pixel grid.

00:00:28.808 --> 00:00:31.158
Enlarge it and pixels grow.

00:00:31.158 --> 00:00:33.507
Edges go jagged and blurry.

00:00:33.507 --> 00:00:34.987
Step four: P O E.

00:00:34.987 --> 00:00:39.077
B, file must shrink: no cause and effect — cut.

00:00:39.077 --> 00:00:42.211
C, colours brighten: no basis — cut.

00:00:42.211 --> 00:00:46.736
D, sharp like vector: confuses it with vector — cut.

00:00:46.736 --> 00:00:54.482
Step five: sanity check and lock. Enlarging a pixel grid shows jagged edges — consistent.

00:00:54.482 --> 00:00:56.832
So the correct answer is A.
